,"comment_lines":["[][196]"],"review_comment":["Do you think there is a chance we could have `Row` implement `SurrogateLogicalPlan` in a follow up? So that `Row` only exists directly after parsing and is turned into a local relation ASAP - while also making this new cleanup rule obsolete?","This is a nice idea, but the issue is that the substitutions happen too early -- all the evaluation of what can be in ROW happens only later. If ROW was a source _only_, we could have given rid of it directly after parsing. But since we allow expressions within it, we need to have `Row` go through \"Operator Optimization\" batch (so \"EVAL\" it)."],"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizer.java","id":37254,"created_at":"2024-11-21T16:55:17Z","original_position":13,"side":"RIGHT","position":13,"submitted_on_commit":"8d3995b9f1458bcb39ce06ca962de538ef1aa7c7","diff_hunk":"@@ -192,6 +193,6 @@ protected static Batch\u003cLogicalPlan\u003e operators() {\n     }\n \n     protected static Batch\u003cLogicalPlan\u003e cleanup() {\n-        return new Batch\u003c\u003e(\"Clean Up\", new ReplaceLimitAndSortAsTopN());\n+        return new Batch\u003c\u003e(\"Clean Up\", new ReplaceLimitAndSortAsTopN(), new ReplaceRowAsLocalRelation());","submitted_line":196},"generatedCommentsNodes":[]}],"coveredGroundTruth":0,"uncoveredGroundTruth":1,"coveredMatchable":6,"uncoveredMatchable":8,"timing":251704,"tokensIn":7922,"tokensOut":8157}